                <pb facs="0746" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg658"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pearson to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-03-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 25,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Pearson reports that the murderer of Labaree, named Seyd Jafer, is
                    identified and located near Mount Ararat on the Turkish frontier. This same man
                    murdered a British subject, and the American and British legations are jointly
                    insisting on energetic action on the part of the Government to bring the
                    murderer to justice. At the request of Mr. Pearson the Persian Government sent
                    stringent telegraphic orders for the protection of Christians.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
